==Russian==

===Etymology 1===

====Pronunciation====
* {{q|phoneme}}
** {{IPA|ru|[v]}}
*** {{audio|ru|Ru-в.ogg}}
** {{IPA|ru|[vʲ]}}
** {{IPA|ru|[f]}}
*** {{audio|ru|Ru-ф.ogg}}
* {{q|letter name}}
** {{ru-IPA|вэ}}
*** {{audio|ru|Ru-03-буква-В.ogg}}

====Letter====
{{letter|ru}}

# {{Cyrl-def|ru|letter|3|вэ}}
#: {{alti|ru|ѵ|tr=v|q=archaic}}

=====See also=====
{{list:Cyrillic script letters/ru}}

====References====
* {{R:ru:Dal}}

===Etymology 2===
{{PIE word|ru|h₁en}}
{{ety|ru|id=in|:inh|orv:въ|tree=1}}
{{inh+|ru|orv|въ}}, from {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*vъ(n)}}, from {{der|ru|ine-pro|*h₁n̥}}, zero-grade form of {{m|ine-pro|*h₁én}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|ru|въ||ru-PRO}}
* {{alter|ru|во||used before certain consonant clusters}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{ru-IPA|в/}} {{q|before vowels and voiced consonants}}
* {{ru-IPA|ф}} {{q|before voiceless consonants}}
* {{ru-IPA|вə}} {{q|when pausing to think}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-в.ogg}}

====Preposition====
{{head|ru|preposition}}

# {{+obj|ru|prep|catpos=prep}}
## ''(location)'' [[in]], [[at]], [[on]]
##: {{uxi|ru|[[он|Он]] '''в''' [[театр|теа́тре]]|He’s '''at''' ('''in''') the theater.}}
# {{+obj|ru|acc|catpos=prep}}
## ''(direction)'' [[to]], [[into]]
##: {{uxi|ru|[[он|Он]] [[идти|идёт]] '''в''' [[теа́тр]]|He’s going '''to''' ('''into''') the theater.}}
## ''(time)'' [[at]], [[in]], [[on]]
##: {{uxi|ru|'''в''' [[три]] [[час|часа́]]|'''at''' three o’clock}}
##: {{uxi|ru|'''в''' [[час|часа́]] [[три]] |'''at''' about three o'clock}}
##: {{uxi|ru|'''в''' [[пятница|пя́тницу]]|'''on''' Friday}}
## [[per]]
##: {{uxi|ru|[[три]] [[раз|ра́за]] '''в''' [[день]]|three times '''per''' day}}
##: {{uxi|ru|[[раз|ра́за]] [[три]] '''в''' [[день]]|about three times '''per''' day}}
## ''(indicating aim or purpose)'' [[for]], [[as]]
##: {{uxi|ru|[[сказа́ть]] '''в''' [[шу́тка|шу́тку]]|say '''as''' a joke}}
## ''(indicating exact correspondence, equivalence)'' [[for]]
##: {{uxi|ru|[[оди́н]] '''в''' [[оди́н]]|one '''for''' one}}
##: {{uxi|ru|[[копе́йка]] '''в''' [[копейка|копе́йку]]|dollar '''for''' dollar|lit=kopeck '''for''' kopeck}}
##: {{uxi|ru|[[душа́]] '''в''' [[душа|ду́шу]]|in perfect harmony|lit=soul '''for''' soul}}
# {{+obj|ru|nom|catpos=prep}}
## ''(indicating becoming, joining)'' [[as]]
##: {{uxi|ru|[[идти́]] '''в''' [[гость|го́сти]]|to visit|lit=to go '''as''' guests}}
##: {{uxi|ru|[[идти́]] '''в''' [[бандит|банди́ты]]|to become a bandit/bandits|lit=to go '''as''' bandits}}
##: {{uxi|ru|[[пойти́]] '''в''' [[политик|поли́тики]]|to enter politics|lit=to go '''as''' politicians}}
##: {{uxi|ru|[[выйти́]] '''в''' [[рабо́чие]]|to join the workforce|lit=to exit '''as''' workers}}
##: {{uxi|ru|[[выйти́]] '''в''' [[человек|лю́ди]]|to go out|lit=to leave '''as''' people}}
##: {{uxi|ru|[[про́чить]] [[кто-то|кого-то]] '''в''' [[начальник|нача́льники]] ([[наследник|насле́дники]])|to expect someone to become the boss (the heir)|lit=to expect '''as''' bosses (heirs)}}
##: {{uxi|ru|[[уйти́]] '''в''' [[профессионал|профессиона́лы]]|to go pro/professional|lit=to leave '''as''' professionals}}
##: {{uxi|ru|[[переквалифици́роваться]] '''в''' [[управдом|управдо́мы]]|to retrain '''as''' a building superintendent}}
##: {{uxi|ru|[[оста́вить]] [[себя́]] '''в''' [[заложник|зало́жники]]|to become a hostage|lit=to leave oneself '''as''' hostages}}
##: {{uxi|ru|[[вы́брать]] ([[себя|себе́]]) '''в''' [[муж|мужья́]]/[[жена|жёны]]/[[супруг|супру́ги]]|to choose a husband/wife/spouse (for oneself)|lit=to choose (for oneself) '''as''' husbands/wives/spouses}}
##: {{uxi|ru|[[взять]] '''в''' [[жена|жёны]]|to take '''as''' a wife}}
##: {{uxi|ru|[[бежа́ть]] '''в''' [[монахиня|мона́хини]]|to run away to become a nun|lit=to flee '''as''' nuns}}
##: {{uxi|ru|[[пода́ться]] '''в''' [[бес|бе́сы]]|to become a demon/demons|lit=to give in '''as''' demons}}

=====Usage notes=====
* The alternative form {{l|ru|во}} is used before some awkward consonant clusters, such as {{lang|ru|во [[второй|второ́м]], во [[вторник|вто́рник]], во [[Флорида|Флори́де]]}}.
* Sense 3 of '''в''' is one of only two environments in Russian in which a preposition takes a nominative argument; the other is [[что за|что́ за]].

=====Related terms=====
* {{l|ru|в-}}, {{l|ru|во-}}

